80 17592186045585 true] [17592186226239 1063 #edb/ref 17592186225342 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226240 1064 "In this lesson, we’ll practice applying the zero-product rule to solve quadratic equations." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226240 1065 13654 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226240 1066 #uuid "8551cef0-52a7-5521-b036-72ac43a7208d" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226240 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226241 1064 "On the math section of the SAT exam, we may face quadratics that don’t easily factor. In such cases, developing fluency with the quadratic formula can save crucial time.\n\nBelow, we'll practice writing quadratic equations in standard form and applying the quadratic formula." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226241 1065 13655 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226241 1066 #uuid "94b79b16-b4c2-597e-bfae-827666cddd5a" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226241 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226242 1064 "Vieta’s formulas are often helpful in algebra problems that ask for the sum or product of roots of a quadratic equation, but don't require the roots themselves. By utilizing Vieta's formulas, we can solve these problems quickly and avoid lengthy computations.\n\nIn this topic, we'll practice applying these formulas, helping us master one of the quickest shortcuts in quadratic problem-solving." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226242 1065 13656 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226242 1066 #uuid "d6b26a01-4a1a-5548-bed9-948ed515f776" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226242 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226243 1064 "Trigonometry problems sometimes require us to find a missing side or trigonometric ratio when only two sides of a right triangle are given. These questions test the ability to connect the Pythagorean theorem with sine, cosine, and tangent definitions.\n\nIn this lesson, we’ll practice using the Pythagorean theorem to complete missing triangle information and then find trigonometric ratios." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226243 1065 13679 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226243 1066 #uuid "030c8a1c-5b49-5037-ac12-a35872a1b646" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226243 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226244 1064 "Problems involving special triangles (equilateral, isosceles right, and $30^\\circ$–$60^\\circ$–$90^\\circ$ triangles) are common in both geometry and coordinate setups.\n\nHere, we’ll practice recognizing these triangle types and apply their relationships to find unknown sides, heights, and areas." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226244 1065 13684 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226244 1066 #uuid "5fa5b8ae-793d-59ce-9037-0ebb2e0dd185" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226244 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226245 1064 "Sometimes, we may encounter multi-step geometry problems that require using similar triangles and trigonometric ratios together to find missing sides or distances.\n\nIn this topic, we’ll get hands-on practice setting up proportions, applying trigonometric ratios, and solving for unknowns." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226245 1065 13692 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226245 1066 #uuid "030c391f-b2ea-578f-add5-4e4d02a2085e" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226245 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226246 1064 "Questions that require adding or subtracting rational expressions with variables and common factors in their denominators test fluency in recognizing common factors. In this topic, we’ll practice combining rational expressions involving common monomial and binomial denominators, including cases where we must first factor some of the denominators." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226246 1065 13883 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226246 1066 #uuid "e9181b21-078a-5f15-ada3-54b45391d4ee" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226246 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226247 1064 "Simplifying rational expressions using polynomial factorization tests our ability to spot, factor, and cancel common polynomial terms.\n\nIn this topic, we’ll practice simplifying rational expressions by factoring trinomials, differences of squares, and common binomials." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226247 1065 13884 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226247 1066 #uuid "9d789480-0a06-5e0a-bb54-d354b0cd1827" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226247 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226248 1064 "In this topic, we'll practice identifying exponential functions from tabular data. In some cases, the base of the function may be a decimal or defined in terms of a parameter." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226248 1065 13924 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226248 1066 #uuid "e5fabeb7-7c51-571c-b0a4-c03e83693e20" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226248 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226249 1064 "Questions involving tables of values often test whether we can recover a quadratic pattern from data.\n\nIn this lesson, we’ll practice interpreting tabular data to determine equations of quadratic functions and their key features." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226249 1065 13927 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226249 1066 #uuid "a1b71dee-f01e-5206-8d16-bc2db667c9c6" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226249 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226250 1064 "This topic provides practice in solving rational equations using three methods: cancelling common factors, applying the flip method, and multiplying through by the lowest common denominator." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226250 1065 13984 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226250 1066 #uuid "50386901-9434-5243-844b-2402b0821fe2" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226250 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226251 1064 "This topic focuses on practicing solving radical equations, including cases where the radical must be isolated first and where variables appear on both sides. We'll also practice finding unknown parameters that result in exactly one real solution." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226251 1065 13985 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226251 1066 #uuid "a467098e-2fb5-5a6b-8e85-f109ec0e7692" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226251 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226252 1064 "This topic helps us build proficiency in solving equations containing multiple radicals. The key idea is to write the equation in such a way that squaring both sides eliminates the radicals. In some cases, we will find a solution in terms of an unknown parameter." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226252 1065 13992 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226252 1066 #uuid "d56750bc-acf2-53e8-b12d-0cd2f47ef51e" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226252 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226253 1064 "In this topic, we'll practice evaluating simple cubic functions and use our knowledge of $n$th root equations to find the input of a cubic that produces a given output." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226253 1065 13994 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226253 1066 #uuid "51454b69-1f9a-592d-8fc0-8478bdbc69a5" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226253 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226254 1064 "This topic provides practice in analyzing absolute value functions. In particular, we'll evaluate these functions, determine inputs for given function outputs, and find unknown constants or parameters in related equations." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226254 1065 13995 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226254 1066 #uuid "aa576bc6-4b4a-5d63-8f6a-d69e341dd75d" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226254 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226255 1064 "This topic provides practice in evaluating and analyzing rational functions. We'll determine outputs of rational expressions, identify the equations of shifted reciprocal functions, and recognize how transformations affect their graphs." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226255 1065 13996 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226255 1066 #uuid "9ab69683-8845-5ae1-8caa-aec18292b913" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226255 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226256 1064 "This topic provides practice in analyzing exponential functions by evaluating them for given inputs, identifying y-intercepts, interpreting tables of values, and recognizing their graphical representations." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226256 1065 13998 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226256 1066 #uuid "fae4e7aa-2941-5260-9ae5-6fe5e52eb455" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226256 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226257 1064 "Questions about graphs of quadratic functions commonly ask to recognize key features like intercepts and the vertex from a graph or equation.\n\nIn this lesson, we'll practice spotting these patterns." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226257 1065 14038 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226257 1066 #uuid "0dc7fe6e-974a-5351-a9a0-f616972eed87" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226257 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226258 1064 "A typical question type on the SAT math section involves interpreting key features of graphs in real-world contexts.\n\nIn this topic, we will practice determining the meaning of points and interpreting the $x$- and $y$-intercepts in terms of the situation they represent." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226258 1065 14039 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226258 1066 #uuid "2b447923-00a7-5a53-94c7-2c6805ed1823" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226258 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226259 1064 "The math section of the SAT includes questions that require us to interpret graphs modeling real-world relationships.\n\nIn this topic, we'll practice identifying points corresponding to specific descriptions, determining initial values, recognizing intervals where a function increases or decreases, and describing changes in a function’s value based on its graph." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226259 1065 14042 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226259 1066 #uuid "6f805e8f-d93c-5c9c-8532-7570818f5cc4" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226259 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226260 1064 "This topic provides practice in solving systems composed of a quadratic equation and a linear equation." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226260 1065 14058 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226260 1066 #uuid "2b67e980-2321-5384-8d58-ae3683995961" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226260 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226261 1064 "In this topic, we'll focus on solving challenging systems composed of a quadratic equation and a linear equation." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226261 1065 14062 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226261 1066 #uuid "de1a7c36-f200-5a35-ab07-1023ee72a3d7" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226261 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226262 1064 "In this topic, we'll strengthen our ability to solve multivariable rational equations. We will use cross-multiplication, isolate variables appearing in numerators and denominators, and handle equations containing several rational terms." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226262 1065 14070 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226262 1066 #uuid "20aea811-7f3e-5676-8ade-fbe1a4277242" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226262 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226263 1064 "This topic focuses on solving multivariable equations that require two or three steps to isolate a chosen variable." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226263 1065 14072 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226263 1066 #uuid "eaa7236a-6ba0-5059-b39b-5fb652910394" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226263 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226264 1064 "In this topic, we will practice constructing exponential models from descriptions involving doubling times, percentage increases, and growth rates greater than 100 percent, and evaluating these models for given inputs." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226264 1065 14076 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226264 1066 #uuid "3a2fdf5b-15ac-5646-9054-cd6de882c4ee" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226264 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226265 1064 "After solving exponential models for the growth rate or the initial value, we'll now focus on solving for time. In particular, we'll practice calculating how long it takes for quantities to double or triple, identifying exponential equations given in context, and finding unknown times from tables or given models." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226265 1065 14079 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226265 1066 #uuid "fdcc0b96-00c4-5809-985c-f620dd831e06" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226265 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226266 1064 "In this topic, we will practice writing and evaluating equations representing percentage decreases, half-lives, and other decay rates in real-world situations. Some questions will also involve determining unknown decay rates or modeling vertically shifted decay functions." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226266 1065 14085 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226266 1066 #uuid "cc9fd89a-73e4-5b9d-8a39-3c85eeb9e11d" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226266 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226267 1064 "A common theme on the math section of the SAT is working with exponential models that contain unknown parameters, such as the growth rate or the initial value. In this topic, we'll practice solving for these unknowns given a description of a real-world situation." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226267 1065 14086 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226267 1066 #uuid "5aa8da43-f5aa-5740-943e-4c952420ec10" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226267 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226268 1064 "In this topic, we'll practice transforming exponential functions, rewriting the transformed functions using the laws of exponents." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226268 1065 14089 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226268 1066 #uuid "81cb3b69-52da-5bde-863c-86af1f1fb80a" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226268 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226269 1064 "Another common theme in the math section of the SAT is constructing exponential functions from a given description. Here, we'll practice building exponential models from descriptions that include initial values, growth factors, or percentage decreases." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226269 1065 14092 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226269 1066 #uuid "05a9f318-cec2-5fed-8b2b-1556071c3e2b" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226269 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226270 1064 "Questions that ask you to determine inputs for a given output in quadratic functions are a common feature of the math section of the SAT. In this lesson, we'll gain valuable practice with these problems." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226270 1065 14094 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226270 1066 #uuid "375001fd-af4d-5b68-94a7-38f047386c67" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226270 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226271 1064 "Quadratic models describing real-world phenomena often have specific features that can be interpreted.\n\nIn this topic, we'll practice translating quadratic models into plain-English statements." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226271 1065 14095 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226271 1066 #uuid "b454b9db-cee9-505a-a69a-d521156b52cb" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226271 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226272 1064 "Geometry problems that involve dimensions, area, or perimeter often lead to quadratic equations.\n\nIn this lesson, we'll practice translating geometric descriptions into quadratic equations and solving them." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226272 1065 14096 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226272 1066 #uuid "0e31aa44-70c2-5650-b14a-91629020bb7b" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226272 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226273 1064 "Questions about extreme values of quadratic functions in standard form often test whether we know how to find a vertex.\n\nIn this lesson, we’ll practice the efficient application of the vertex formula." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226273 1065 14099 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226273 1066 #uuid "57abe12b-68bb-5ee1-810e-6d4eacc77bbf" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226273 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226274 1064 "Problems involving extreme values of quadratic functions often test whether we can quickly identify the vertex of a parabola from its factored form.\n\nHere, we’ll practice efficiently locating maximums and minimums of quadratic functions presented in factored form." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226274 1065 14101 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226274 1066 #uuid "153165ad-4548-5dd5-bcaa-5da0e7b80727" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226274 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226275 1064 "Problems that relate two or more numbers through multiplication or addition often lead to quadratic equations. These problems test our ability to translate a word problem into a quadratic equation and solve it.\n\nIn this lesson, we'll practice forming and solving quadratic equations that model number relationships. The resulting quadratic equations typically have quite large coefficients, which often make the quadratic formula an efficient solution method." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226275 1065 14106 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226275 1066 #uuid "7ac3f900-3c0e-575d-93f7-cfcd9134ae54" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226275 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226276 1064 "When presented with real-world data on vertical motion, we can often fit it to a quadratic model using vertex form. In this topic, we'll practice doing just that." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226276 1065 14107 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226276 1066 #uuid "62d5b0f8-5328-50f1-9768-d5bda692b5ca" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226276 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226277 1064 "Questions about multiplying binomials test the fluency with the distributive property and the ability to organize terms correctly to avoid sign or arithmetic errors.\n\nIn this lesson, we’ll practice expanding products of binomials of different forms, simplifying the results, and matching coefficients or terms to solve for unknown values." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226277 1065 14110 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226277 1066 #uuid "bbc3c7f8-cefd-5d53-b6b5-d91a1aa186b0" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226277 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226278 1064 "Questions involving distributive laws often appear on the math section of the SAT exam. These questions check whether we can correctly expand, combine, and simplify expressions.\n\nHere, we’ll practice applying the distributive property to polynomial expressions, simplifying them, and identifying or comparing coefficients to find missing values." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226278 1065 14116 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226278 1066 #uuid "6be56b30-1957-5ae3-86a7-1dd371fb7bef" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226278 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226279 1064 "The difference of squares formula often appears in questions that require quick recognition of algebraic patterns.\n\nIn this lesson, we’ll practice identifying and factoring differences of squares, including cases with coefficients, fractions, and multiple variables." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226279 1065 14121 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226279 1066 #uuid "ae45bcb7-0fdf-5423-9214-1eadd7a9ade1" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226279 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226280 1064 "Factoring by a greatest common factor (GCF) is often used as a step in solving problems that contain polynomial expressions.\n\nIn this topic, we'll practice spotting numeric and variable GCFs in polynomials and using them to factor the expressions." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226280 1065 14123 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226280 1066 #uuid "16a0f3d0-db8d-51bc-b9fb-402038037687" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226280 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226281 1064 "Questions involving factoring trinomials are common on the math section of the SAT exam. Recognizing the corresponding patterns can help us solve equations and simplify expressions.\n\nHere, we’ll practice factoring different types of trinomials, including perfect squares and more general quadratic expressions." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226281 1065 14125 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226281 1066 #uuid "44190976-0273-53e5-8dad-2c5c825fc236" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226281 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226282 1064 "Factoring higher-order polynomials tests our ability to recognize patterns beyond simple quadratics.\n\nIn this topic, we’ll practice identifying and factoring polynomial patterns, including higher powers and nested differences of squares." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226282 1065 14127 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226282 1066 #uuid "31e2c190-665d-51f6-84f0-0f41fd6b4481" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226282 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226283 1064 "Problems involving borders or frames often test the ability to express areas with unknown widths using algebraic equations.\n\nIn this topic, we'll practice modeling these geometric relationships and solving for missing dimensions." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226283 1065 14195 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226283 1066 #uuid "415ed7e3-3f37-5344-ba28-1538980b92f4" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226283 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226284 1064 "The math problems often involve modeling area or perimeter using algebraic functions. These questions combine geometric understanding with algebraic manipulation.\n\nMastering this connection between shapes and equations takes practice, but it’s a powerful way to boost both reasoning speed and accuracy when dealing with geometry problems." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226284 1065 14196 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226284 1066 #uuid "9b9a03e2-adbc-5793-92e8-ddc9572fe721" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226284 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226285 1064 "On the math section of the SAT exam, we're often asked to create a function for surface area or volume directly from a description.\n\nIn this topic, we’ll practice constructing and interpreting functions that represent surface area and volume, turning real-world descriptions into precise mathematical formulas." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226285 1065 14197 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226285 1066 #uuid "e43a59d5-a9a4-5f22-97ab-19569dd8228a" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226285 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226286 1064 "Problems involving inscribed squares and circles often test our understanding of how geometric relationships between these shapes connect.\n\nIn this lesson, we’ll practice translating between circle and square parameters (radius, side, area, and circumference) to solve multi-step geometry problems." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226286 1065 14203 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226286 1066 #uuid "524b845c-5174-58a8-8307-df1053dbbb05" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226286 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226287 1064 "On the math section of the SAT exam, questions about circles inscribed in equilateral triangles often depend on 30-60-90 right-triangle reasoning. In this lesson, we’ll practice setting up these relationships and solving problems." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226287 1065 14205 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226287 1066 #uuid "ea67a6b5-a568-5bac-8c20-5bb717e3a367" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226287 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226288 1064 "On the math section of the SAT exam, we’ll often see problems that hide special triangles inside rectangles, squares, or circles. These questions test our ability to spot these special triangles and use their ratios to find unknown lengths or areas.\n\nIn this topic, we'll practice recognizing these patterns and setting up the correct equations." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226288 1065 14207 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226288 1066 #uuid "78b20c0d-8cec-576f-961a-6884bffc31fb" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226288 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226289 1064 "Inscribed‐circle problems often ask us to switch quickly between a circle’s radius or diameter and a square’s side.\n\nIn this lesson, we’ll practice setting up these relationships and solving multi-step geometric problems." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226289 1065 14212 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226289 1066 #uuid "dd78f7d2-f721-50ec-88c1-bc3604d71cb3" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226289 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226290 1064 "Problems involving equilateral triangles inscribed in a circle often boil down to recalling 30-60-90 triangle facts.\n\nIn this lesson, we’ll practice setting up these relationships and solving related problems." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226290 1065 14213 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226290 1066 #uuid "093ab10a-06f0-5a7d-a120-3b0a1abefe59" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226290 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226291 1064 "The math section of the SAT exam sometimes asks to evaluate simple trigonometric functions at large angles. These evaluations are made by reducing the argument of the trigonometric function using periodicity.\n\nIn this lesson, we’ll practice reducing large angles to their coterminal or reference angles, identifying the relevant quadrants, and determining the correct sign and value of the trigonometric ratio." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226291 1065 14214 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226291 1066 #uuid "12690ee9-cf72-58c1-8684-08c7d026bb82" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226291 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226292 1064 "Questions that require us to solve quadratic equations with unknown parameters show up regularly on the math section of the SAT exam.\n\nIn this topic, we'll build speed by practicing systematic moves for solving these kinds of problems." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226292 1065 14231 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226292 1066 #uuid "c68eafbc-fee7-5797-95dd-7a13cb017b47" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226292 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226293 1064 "Solving quadratic equations by factoring tests the ability to recognize when a quadratic can be factored quickly into linear factors.\n\nIn this lesson, we’ll practice rewriting, factoring, and solving quadratic equations efficiently, developing the fluency needed to identify patterns and avoid time-consuming methods like the quadratic formula." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226293 1065 14234 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226293 1066 #uuid "65e3f6f6-fed7-51b6-a061-cb0660beb448" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226293 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226294 1064 "This topic focuses on understanding how the structure of a quadratic expression reveals useful information about its behavior.\n\nBy recognizing connections across different forms, we’ll be able to extract relationships between coefficients, factors, and intercepts." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226294 1065 14235 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226294 1066 #uuid "7382e9f7-c263-595b-8809-703cddf3dd8c" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226294 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226295 1064 "Quadratic equations have exactly one real solution when their discriminant equals zero.\n\nIn this topic, we'll practice identifying and using this condition." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226295 1065 14236 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226295 1066 #uuid "d7667317-b6df-5d07-828e-898e0f1c1c92" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226295 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226296 1064 "Quadratic equations have real solutions when their discriminant is nonnegative, and *distinct* real solutions when their discriminant is positive.\n\nIn this topic, we'll practice identifying and using these conditions." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226296 1065 14242 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226296 1066 #uuid "0f7b3072-4634-5a4f-9e27-bf793927daee" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226296 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226297 1064 "Quadratic equations have no real solutions when their discriminant is negative.\n\nIn this topic, we'll practice identifying and using this condition." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226297 1065 14243 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226297 1066 #uuid "26d6df50-e383-5480-b7a2-7a75ae373eea" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226297 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226298 1064 "This topic focuses on solving nonlinear equations that involve multiple variables. We'll practice isolating variables in radical and quadratic equations, rearranging formulas, and applying the laws of exponents when working with radicals." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226298 1065 14246 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226298 1066 #uuid "930266f7-b27b-537a-a0cc-c43a2e01f832" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226298 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226299 1064 "In this topic, we'll practice solving systems of nonlinear equations involving square roots, exponentials, and absolute values." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226299 1065 14247 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226299 1066 #uuid "246feaac-a4ca-5fa5-aae9-ca16593ed4f1" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226299 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226300 1064 "An important concept that features in the math section of the SAT exam is identifying when a line and a parabola intersect at exactly one point.\n\nIn this topic, we will determine unknown parameters in quadratic systems with one solution involving horizontal or sloped lines, as well as cases where both linear and quadratic equations within a system contain parameters." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226300 1065 14248 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226300 1066 #uuid "b82af3ab-e2cb-5fd2-8151-06b2d540c7e4" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226300 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226301 1064 "Common questions on the math section of the SAT exam involve working with exponential functions written in equivalent forms.\n\nYou'll need to be able to analyze how different representations display key quantities, such as constant terms, coefficients, or bases, that correspond to the function's maximum, minimum, or given output values." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226301 1065 14249 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226301 1066 #uuid "c56a67e9-d0f8-587c-88b3-f57340aebe80" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226301 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226302 1064 "In this topic, we'll practice converting exponential models to different time units. We will adjust equations to reflect new time measures, compute percentage increases or decreases over specified intervals, and determine time periods associated with particular percentage changes." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226302 1065 14252 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226302 1066 #uuid "0ac0eb87-4a24-599b-8a8e-4bc753e7004d" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226302 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226303 1064 "A common theme on the SAT math section is understanding how exponential functions behave, and this can include cases with restricted domains. In particular, you will need to identify when they have maximum or minimum values, determine their ranges, and describe whether they are increasing or decreasing over those domains." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226303 1065 14255 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226303 1066 #uuid "29988130-0d82-5766-8820-7beb807c8166" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226303 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226304 1064 "A common theme on the math section of the SAT is working with exponential functions that contain one or multiple unknown parameters.\nIn this topic, we'll practice solving for these unknowns using information such as points on the curve or the y-intercept." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226304 1065 14257 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226304 1066 #uuid "551c6b37-617a-51bb-b148-18523095a7f9" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226304 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226305 1064 "In this topic, we'll practice performing horizontal and vertical translations on polynomials." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226305 1065 14263 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226305 1066 #uuid "8e1230bc-2a80-554c-ade1-0d96f98ddf98" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226305 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226306 1064 "Problems involving the symmetry of quadratic functions often test how well we can reason about a parabola without graphing it.\n\nIn this lesson, we’ll practice using these patterns to draw logical conclusions about a quadratic function’s structure and behavior." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226306 1065 14266 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226306 1066 #uuid "f233d7b3-1213-5efe-980a-29d2a1e2b50a" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226306 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226307 1064 "In this topic, we'll use our knowledge of the factor theorem to draw conclusions about unknown coefficients in quadratic equations." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226307 1065 14267 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226307 1066 #uuid "c3907658-6bef-5aff-98a4-679cb0112b74" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226307 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226308 1064 "Questions about quadratic functions in vertex form often focus on identifying or interpreting the maximum or minimum value of a parabola quickly.\n\nBelow, we’ll practice reading vertex form directly and using it to determine both the location and the value of a parabola’s highest or lowest point." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226308 1065 14271 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226308 1066 #uuid "aca635af-cb01-546a-8bbc-57e47a0e6b23" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226308 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226309 1064 "On the math section of the SAT exam, questions that describe physical relationships usually test our ability to translate written definitions into mathematical formulas.\n\nIn this lesson, we’ll practice turning descriptions of physical phenomena into equations, using the given definitions to solve for unknown variables, and reinforcing formula reasoning through applied examples." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226309 1065 14275 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226309 1066 #uuid "e9ab0036-ed27-541d-b911-2dbd532c3c15" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226309 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226310 1064 "In this topic, we will determine unknown parameters in quadratic systems with zero or two solutions involving horizontal or sloped lines, as well as cases where both equations of the system contain parameters." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226310 1065 14283 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226310 1066 #uuid "279c1e34-8942-5a1a-91e9-e43971f48ad9" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226310 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226311 1064 "Solving quadratic equations with leading coefficients by factoring tests the ability to recognize when a quadratic can be factored quickly into linear factors.\n\nIn this lesson, we’ll practice factoring and solving quadratic equations with leading coefficients efficiently, developing the fluency needed to identify patterns and avoid time-consuming methods like the quadratic formula." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226311 1065 14285 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226311 1066 #uuid "1df8890c-b83e-5ac5-84a8-c23dc8604289" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226311 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226312 1064 "In this topic, we'll focus on recognizing and using structure to solve nonlinear systems of equations. We will practice substituting expressions with one or two variables and applying patterns such as the difference of squares to find solutions efficiently." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226312 1065 14286 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226312 1066 #uuid "007d0218-cbde-592f-a3a1-638ea4509656" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226312 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226313 1064 "In this topic, we'll use our knowledge of polynomial graphs to determine their properties, such as the number of roots and valid outputs of polynomials over particular intervals. We'll also practice identifying the factored form of a polynomial from its graph." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226313 1065 14288 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226313 1066 #uuid "e834ca42-6523-5438-b755-9107a6ac34c6" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226313 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226314 1064 "In this topic, we'll use our knowledge of polynomial transformations to identify properties of transformed polynomials, including their roots, vertices, and tables of values." 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226314 1065 14293 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226314 1066 #uuid "e5503279-4009-5ef7-ad63-70ffaa654491" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true] [17592186226314 1067 "Introduction" 13194139533380 17592186045585 true]] :edb/tempids {"__map/00000000000000000000" 17592186222539 "__map/00000000000000000001" 17592186222540 "__map/00000000000000000002" 17592186222541 "__map/00000000000000000003" 17592186222542 "__map/00000000000000000004" 17592186222543 "__map/00000000000000000005" 17592186222544 "__map/00000000000000000006" 17592186222545 "__map/00000000000000000007" 17592186222546 "__map/00000000000000000008" 17592186222547 "__map/00000000000000000009" 17592186222548 "__map/00000000000000000010" 17592186222549 "__map/00000000000000000011" 17592186222550 "__map/00000000000000000012" 17592186222551 "__map/00000000000000000013" 17592186222552 "__map/000000000